Fonts
-----
Inter — SIL Open Font License 1.1, via @fontsource-variable/inter. The only typeface embedded in the
rendered demo, which the OFL permits.

**San Francisco is deliberately not used for any rendered type here.** SF Pro is installed on every Mac
and would be the obvious choice, and the Apple San Francisco Font License (EA1370) grants use "solely
for creating mock-ups of user interfaces" and expressly forbids using the font to "create, develop,
display or otherwise distribute any documentation, artwork, website content or any other work product".
A demo video is a work product, so every caption and keystroke pill here is Inter.

San Francisco does appear in the demo, inside every screenshot and screen recording of the app. That is
macOS drawing its own interface with its own copy of its own font, which is what the licence is for.

Cap — parameters only
---------------------
The Loom-style camera in video/film/src/loom reproduces the motion language of Cap
(github.com/CapSoftware/Cap), whose core is **AGPL-3.0**. Its published constants were read and used as
facts — the 2.0x zoom amount, the -300/+2500 ms segment around a click, the 2500 ms merge gap, the
spring coefficients, the 130 ms click punch, the keystroke-pill geometry. **No Cap code was copied.**
The spring solver here is the closed-form solution of a damped harmonic oscillator, written from the
standard result; the zoom law is a fresh implementation of the documented behaviour.

No Cap binary or source is vendored, invoked or distributed by this repository.

